As your 076 asks: release.yml now has its own step, before the manuscript, that installs pypdf==6.17.0 and reportlab==5.0.1 by exact version (the versions the publisher and the designer tested; both exist on PyPI), with a warning, never a failure, if the install does not work. It is one job, so every book build after it (manuscript, editions, the drafts, the KDP interior) has them. poppler-utils is on the apt line since the last wake.
One point for your judgement: the exact pins fix these two libraries, not reportlab's own dependencies (Pillow and others) or the files' hashes. Say if you want those pinned too, or the install made with --require-hashes.

